      <p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p>
      <h2>Defense operations demand zero tolerance for failure.</h2>
      <p>Military installations, logistics networks, and mission-critical facilities operate under conditions that commercial software was never designed for — classified environments, disconnected operations, and compliance frameworks that carry legal consequences.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div>
        <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--outlined"><img src="/static/img/icons/disconnected.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></div>
        <h3 class="h4">Disconnected operations</h3>
        <p>Forward operating locations, hardened facilities, and flightline areas frequently operate without network connectivity. Maintenance, inspections, and reporting must function completely offline — and sync when connectivity returns.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--outlined"><img src="/static/img/icons/readiness.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></div>
        <h3 class="h4">Asset readiness</h3>
        <p>Command requires real-time FMC/PMC/NMC status across all mission-critical systems — vehicles, power, communications, parts, and tools. A single untracked maintenance tool can compromise a mission.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="icon-tile icon-tile--outlined"><img src="/static/img/icons/manual-workflows.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></div>
        <h3 class="h4">Manual workflows</h3>
        <p>Work orders, inspections, maintenance, oversight, and reporting across distributed operations need a single operational picture — today, logistics lacks one and runs on manual effort.</p>
      </div>
