<section class="section">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Logistics</p>
      <h2>Parts where they need to be. When they need to be there.</h2>
      <p>NMC assets waiting on parts represent the single largest avoidable drag on readiness. Assetas connects maintenance requirements, parts inventory, and supply chain status — so commanders know what is NMC, why, and when it will be back.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="points points--single">
      <li><h3>Parts &amp; inventory management</h3><p>NSN-based inventory tracking, bench stock visibility, and shop stock list management — integrated with unit maintenance operations and connected to DLA supply chain data.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Readiness-to-supply linkage</h3><p>Every NMC asset linked to its outstanding parts requisition. Commanders see — at a glance — what is down, what part is needed, and when it arrives.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Supply chain visibility</h3><p>EDD tracking on all open requisitions, backorder status, and substitute NSN identification — surfaced at the unit level without manual status calls to the supply room.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

